<h1>Pure winter hiking <br><strong>in the Alps</strong></h1>
<p><strong>Winter hiking</strong> means experiencing the Alpine winter in its most original rhythm. And that step by step. It&#39;s not about speed, but about being consciously on the move: the <strong>crunching snow</strong> under your shoes, the <strong>warming sun</strong> on your face, the feeling of peace and space. Winter hiking in <strong>Austria</strong> or snowshoeing in the <strong>Black Forest</strong> offer precisely these quiet moments away from the hustle and bustle. On well-groomed trails, <strong>winter in South Tyrol</strong> also shows its quiet, clear side.</p>
